Secret of magia is and action RPG, and it has some really weird stuff:
- The equipment system that isn't explained, and you basically need to purchase every single weapon to check if your class can equip it;
- The guard feature that works if you have equipped any kind of shield, but lacks of any graphical animation, basically you just sit there and ask yourself whether you are actually guarding or not, and hope for the best;
- The enemies get stronger as your character level up, and even the starting slimes end up almost 1-hit-killing you;
- The knockback that makes you switch areas just as you enter a new map and some monters attack you;
- The knockback that gets you stuck in between a monster and it's own attacks;
- The knockback;
- The doors that have weird hitzones and are sometime placed wrong (for example: doors on the left side that teleport you on a sofa in a room called "the right wing" (?));
- Visual glitches, a lot of them, you can walk on walls in many rooms, windows are placed wrong on the walls, roofs have very unusual shapes (i wanted to take a screenshot to show that, but pressing f12 quits the game, btw);
- Letters that morph into flowers (there is a letter in the first village, and as you try to read it, it switch to a flower, and gets back to a paper sheet as you quit reading it);
- Lack of explanations about the mechanics (it took me some time to figure out how to use the shovel, and i still don't understand what's the point of the lantern and how to use it);
- The story basically doesn't exist, you just start an adventure not knowing what you are doing and why, it just tells you something about some elements you should find;
- Textures in general, they are glitchy and buggy when you get in front of some objects;
- You can't alt-tab during the game, you are just stuck in fullscreen;
At the end, i mjust say that the game isn't really "bad", but it needs A LOT of beta testing and bug fixing, and a plot, too.
